1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Eighty-three percent of music students quit.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Not because they lack talent. Not because they don't practice.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
They quit because they wait seven days between lessons.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Long enough for bad habits to calcify and motivation to die.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Julian Toha's Oclef method proved daily feedback achieves a 91% success rate.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
I built Cadence to deliver that same feedback — free, instant, powered by AI.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
And it actually hears you play.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
This is Cadence. Every element designed around the piano — black keys, white keys, gold pedals.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
First, tell Cadence who you are: beginner learning to read, intermediate learning to practice,

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
advanced learning to perform, or apprentice learning to build.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Every response adapts to your stage. Built-in Kaizen timer — fifteen focused minutes.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
And every coaching response is powered by Featherless AI running DeepSeek V3 —

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
primary AI coach, not a backup.

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Integrated for Iris Hacks IV bonus points.

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Meet Maria. Twelve years old. Three weeks into piano. Her teacher sees her on Thursdays. Today is Monday.

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
She records herself playing her C major scale. Cadence performs real-time FFT note detection.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Hann windowing, harmonic structure validation, MIDI frequency mapping.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Seven of eight notes identified. Tempo: ~120 BPM.

19
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Then Maria tells Cadence what felt hard.

20
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
"Going up is fine, but on the way down my fingers get all tangled at the thumb crossover."

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Cadence combines the audio analysis with Maria's description and responds.

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Not "practice more." Not generic encouragement. The 80/20 method: isolate the ONE thing.

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The same feedback a $60-an-hour teacher would give. But Maria got it on a Monday, two minutes after she practiced.

24
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Cadence also sees your sheet music. Upload any photo — vision AI analyzes it instantly.

25
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Key signature, time signature, hardest section, specific practice strategy — all from a photo.

26
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Every session builds your progress. 22-day streak. 47 sessions. Six achievement badges.

27
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Skills Genome radar tracking seven dimensions of musical growth. Practice heatmap showing every day you showed up.

28
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
And here's what makes Cadence different: it won't lie to you.

29
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
If you record silence, it tells you honestly — no music detected.

30
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Harmonic structure analysis distinguishes real struck strings from voice, noise, and percussion.

31
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Only real piano notes reach the AI coach. No fabricated feedback. No hallucinated mistakes.

32
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Cadence closes the seven-day feedback gap. Every practice session becomes a lesson.

33
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Every mistake becomes data. Every student gets a world-class piano coach in their pocket.

34
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Try it live at the link below — powered by Featherless AI. Your coach is waiting.

35
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The instrument is the gym. And every day you don't have a coach is a day the neural pathway doesn't get built.
